title ALES19 — Lotus's scrub window, a small movable read dragged across a stereo master
prompt Autonomous loop past REMEMBER + the itineraries — take the next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first, self-approve the design round, send each finished increment, stop at the custody gates. baton prin recur.
think ALES18 (the live loop meter) landed and its road-on named a scrub window as the next want: a small movable read a keeper drags across a master. Crux-first: a scrub is a POSITIONED READ — seek the ALES15 head to the window start, read exactly the window length — so it needs no new transport and no new arithmetic, only the recognition that a draggable window is a seek plus a bounded block. Highest-Lindy (editing is done on every session for years), most-tractable, and wholly within the read side (no module seam, no gate). A punch region tying playback to the Mikrophone capture stays a seam that waits for Keaton's word, so I deliberately did NOT take it.
think The crux and why it is EXACT: a scrub window read at position p returns exactly the master slice [p, p+n), n = min(win, len−p). Two facts. A scrub is a seek-then-read — the window is ALES15's read_block off a head seeded at p, so its bytes are the master's own by ALES15's already-proven copy. And consecutive windows TILE — windows at 0, L, 2L, … are disjoint half-open intervals whose union is [0, len), so dragging a scrub of length L in steps of L concatenates back to EACH channel byte-for-byte, the last window honestly short and a window at the end empty. Composing ALES17, meter_window equals metering the master slice directly — the level under the drag is the true level of what the window covers.
think Reuse over reinvention: stereo_transport.read_block and stereo_meter.StereoMeter/feed/peak_*/rms_* reused whole; the only new code is the held Scrub (pos + fixed win), make (BadWindow bound), move_to (PastEnd), nudge (signed i64 drag clamped to [0,len]), read_window (seek-then-read into matched buffers), and meter_window (the window slice fed to a fresh StereoMeter). The window length is bounded at make to max_scrub_window = timeline.max_clip ≤ meter.max_meter_samples, so meter_window cannot overflow — the one place a scrub's legality is proven, letting meter_window use `feed catch unreachable` honestly.
think Width discipline: nudge carries the drag in i64 (pos ≤ 2^32, |delta| ≤ 2^31, so the sum cannot wrap), clamps to [0, len], and @intCast back to u32 only after the clamp bounds it. No usize in authored surface. GREEN on the FIRST build.
obs GREEN on the first build across seven blocks: tiling at L of 1,2,3,5 concatenated each channel byte-for-byte (last window short, end window empty); an arbitrary positioned read returned its exact slice (mid [2,5) and a short tail [4,6)); meter_window matched a reference StereoMeter fed the raw slice per channel; nudge clamped an overshoot low to 0 and high to len, a drag left-then-right landing on a covered window; a power-rendered center pan scrubbed 700 per side, metered peak and DC rms 700; scrubbing and metering mutated neither channel; make refused BadWindow (zero and oversized), move_to refused PastEnd, read_window refused BadBlock.
obs tame_style_check exit 0 (bans clean, no scrub-specific ban); width-check clean; the new module carries many asserts, off the zero-assert ratchet.
loom witness=ales_scrub_witness cases=7 tile_lengths=4 result=GREEN build=first-try
